# todo.aide — writeMethodology

Audit against `src/tools/init/writeMethodology/.aide`. The spec's target
state is "composes the methodology block from canonical docs read
through initContent at runtime, never from literals in this file".
The current implementation calls `getMethodology()` from initContent,
which itself returns a literal — so this helper is a literal-consumer
by proxy. Once `initContent` is refactored (see its own todo.aide),
this helper must switch to the new disk-backed interface.

Fix agents: work one item per session. Depends on
`src/tools/init/initContent/todo.aide` being fully green first — do
not start this file's items until initContent reads from `docs/`.

## Issues

- [ ] **src/tools/init/writeMethodology/index.ts** — the helper calls
      `getMethodology()` from initContent, which returns a literal.
      After initContent is refactored to read from `docs/`, switch to
      the new lookup-by-name interface and compose the methodology
      block from the bytes returned by the disk-backed reader. The
      composition (header + marker + body + marker) stays here; the
      source of the body moves entirely to `docs/`. Violates
      `outcomes.desired` #1 ("faithful render of canonical docs read
      from docs/ at runtime").

- [ ] **src/tools/init/writeMethodology/index.ts** — `getMethodologyMarker()`
      is imported from initContent and used as the idempotency check.
      This can stay — the marker is a framework-shape concern, not
      AIDE doctrine — but confirm during the fix that the marker text
      remains stable across the initContent refactor so existing host
      projects that have already been initialized still match on
      re-runs. A marker change would break idempotency on every
      existing install.

- [ ] **src/tools/init/writeMethodology/index.ts** — after the switch,
      add coverage that fails if the installed block contains the
      string "Intel-Driven" (the old wording). This is a narrow
      regression guard against reintroducing a literal fallback,
      because the exact drift we are fixing is textually detectable.
      The broader guard — no AIDE doctrine strings in this file's
      source — lives in the cross-cutting regression test tracked in
      `scaffoldCommands/todo.aide`.
